*> Corrigé TP3.2 : atelier chaînes
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. TP32.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-LIGNE-SRC  PIC X(40) VALUE "martin;SOPHIE;lyon".
01 WS-NOM        PIC X(15).
01 WS-PRENOM     PIC X(15).
01 WS-VILLE      PIC X(15).
01 WS-SORTIE     PIC X(60).
01 WS-MOT        PIC X(30).
01 WS-MOT-MAJ    PIC X(30).
01 WS-PHRASE     PIC X(60).
01 WS-NB-VOYELLES PIC 99.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
0000-PRINCIPAL.
    PERFORM 1000-IDENTITE
    PERFORM 2000-PALINDROME
    PERFORM 3000-VOYELLES
    STOP RUN.

1000-IDENTITE.
    UNSTRING WS-LIGNE-SRC DELIMITED BY ";"
        INTO WS-NOM WS-PRENOM WS-VILLE
    END-UNSTRING
    *> Nom en majuscules
    MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-NOM) TO WS-NOM
    *> Prénom : tout en minuscules puis initiale en majuscule
    MOVE FUNCTION LOWER-CASE(WS-PRENOM) TO WS-PRENOM
    MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-PRENOM(1:1)) TO WS-PRENOM(1:1)
    *> Ville : idem
    MOVE FUNCTION LOWER-CASE(WS-VILLE) TO WS-VILLE
    MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-VILLE(1:1)) TO WS-VILLE(1:1)

    MOVE SPACES TO WS-SORTIE
    STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-PRENOM) DELIMITED BY SIZE
           " "                      DELIMITED BY SIZE
           FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NOM)    DELIMITED BY SIZE
           ", "                     DELIMITED BY SIZE
           FUNCTION TRIM(WS-VILLE)  DELIMITED BY SIZE
        INTO WS-SORTIE
    END-STRING
    DISPLAY "Identite : " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SORTIE).

2000-PALINDROME.
    DISPLAY "Un mot ? " WITH NO ADVANCING
    ACCEPT WS-MOT
    MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MOT)) TO WS-MOT-MAJ
    IF FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MOT-MAJ) =
       FUNCTION REVERSE(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MOT-MAJ))
        DISPLAY FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MOT) " est un palindrome"
    ELSE
        DISPLAY FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MOT) " n'est pas un palindrome"
    END-IF.

3000-VOYELLES.
    DISPLAY "Une phrase ? " WITH NO ADVANCING
    ACCEPT WS-PHRASE
    MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-PHRASE) TO WS-PHRASE
    MOVE 0 TO WS-NB-VOYELLES
    INSPECT WS-PHRASE TALLYING WS-NB-VOYELLES
        FOR ALL "A" ALL "E" ALL "I" ALL "O" ALL "U" ALL "Y"
    DISPLAY "Nombre de voyelles : " WS-NB-VOYELLES.
